{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Until I come to my lord, to Seir.</b> When Jacob returned to his land, his route passed through the land of Seir. Now Esau said to him, 'I will go before you,' meaning that he would not part from him until he returned to his father, to do him honor upon arriving in his land. But Jacob said: I will proceed slowly, and my lord may return to his seat of government; and if I come by way of his city, he will honor me and go with me as he pleases. This was not a vow on Jacob's part that he would come to him, for Esau had no need of it. And our Sages said further (Avodah Zarah 25a) that it was not in Jacob's mind to go by way of Seir at all, and his intention was to distance himself from him as much as he could; but he broadened the way for him, and this too was wise counsel. And they have yet another midrash (Bereshit Rabbah 78:14), that he will fulfill his word in the days of the Messiah, as it is written (Obadiah 1:21), 'And saviors shall go up on Mount Zion to judge the Mount of Esau' — he says that the saviors who are on Mount Zion will go up to judge the Mount of Esau."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:39:06.612993115Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}